§ CSLv3 2D OPERATORS
I> reconciled: pasted (Peirce+tensor+Feynman), root (Peirce linearized)
R! ← Peirce Existential Graphs: enclosure = negation, juxtaposition = AND
R! ← Penrose/tensor diagrams: spatial = structural
R! ← Feynman: time-axis implicit in layout

§ ENCLOSURE SEMANTICS
  ( X )           → grouping (binding)
  [ X ]           → list / array / sequence
  { X }           → set / block / scope
  ⟨ X ⟩           → tuple / record / entity-property
  ⟦ X ⟧           → formula / equation / meaning-of
  « X »           → quotation (X mentioned, ¬ used) / external API
  ⌈ X ⌉           → constraint / upper-bound / invariant / postcondition
  ⌊ X ⌋           → floor / lower-bound / precondition
  ⟪ X ⟫           → temporal scope / phase marker

§ LINEARIZED PEIRCEAN LOGIC
I> from v2-root: indentation = cut depth (negation/scope boundary)
I> adjacency = conjunction (co-present on sheet)
  
  indent = scope → deeper indent = nested assertion
  adjacent items at same indent = AND'd
  
  ex:
    §material.property:
      ρ : f32 ⌈0.01..20000⌉
      μ : f32 ⌈0..1⌉
      σ : [f32;6]
        ¬σ < 0 @compression     # indent = Peircean cut = negation scope

    §chunk ⊞32³ voxel*           # adjacent = all true simultaneously

§ PEIRCE ENCLOSURE → NEGATION (optional mode)
  ¬(X)   ≡ Peircean cut of X
  double-cut: ¬(¬(X)) = X       # insertion/erasure rule
  scroll: ¬(P ¬(Q)) ≡ P ⇒ Q    # implication via nested cuts
  R! use when proof-theoretic rigor needed; normal specs use → ⇒

§ TENSOR/STRING DIAGRAMS (ASCII form)
I> from pasted: for multi-input operations
  X ─f→ Y ─g→ Z        # f:X→Y, g:Y→Z, sequential composition
  X ═╗
      ╠ h → W           # h: X⊗Y → W, parallel inputs merge
  Y ═╝

  R! use when composition structure > prose description
  R! use in §05 REASON blocks for causal structure

§ DATAFLOW (Feynman-style)
  vertical   = time (top → bottom)
  horizontal = parallel computation
  labels on edges = typed values
  vertices   = operations
  
  R! use in reasoning blocks when causal structure > linear prose

§ TABLES (2D as pure information)
  | col1 | col2 | col3 |
  |------|------|------|
  | ...  | ...  | ...  |
  R! use when data is genuinely 2D
  N! linearize tables into prose

§ CONDITIONAL PATTERNS (from v2-root)
  simple:    ⟨entity.health⟩ ≤ 0 → die
  gated:     W! §physics.tick @frame
  warning:   ⚠ §render.pass # > 4 → perf-warn
  query:     Q? §audio.reverb.quality
  block:
    ⟨player.underwater⟩:
      §render.post += fog-underwater
      §audio.filter : lowpass@800hz
      ⟨breath⟩ -= Δt
∎
